# A stage0 sample: maps with String keys, through the host's map. It counts
# words in a map of numbers (putting a key again replaces its value), keeps
# records holding text in a second map (the text is copied into the map's
# region), reads them back by key, branches on a missing key, removes one,
# and walks a map's keys with `forEach` in the order they were first put. It
# exits with code 0:
#
#   the: 3
#   cat: 1
#   keys: 4
#   no dog
#   counted: the cat sat mat
#   Ada is 36, likes tea
#   Linus is 54, likes coffee
#   removed Ada: 1
#   no Ada
maps is module
maps purpose "Count words in a map and keep records by name in another"
maps path maps
maps imports standard.console
maps imports standard.math
maps imports standard.map
maps imports standard.string
maps exports main

stdoutWriter is capability
stdoutWriter purpose "Authority to write lines to standard output"
stdoutWriter grants write console.stdout none

Person is record
Person purpose "Someone's age and favourite drink"
Person typeParameter none
Person field age Int64
Person field drink String

Counts is typeInstance
Counts purpose "How many times each word was seen"
Counts in none
Counts instantiates map.Map String Int64

People is typeInstance
People purpose "People by name"
People in none
People instantiates map.Map String Person

